---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const description =
  "How UniRepository sources university facts, what we refuse to invent, and how GCU prose is generated and validated.";
---

<Base title="Methodology" description={description}>
  <div class="doc mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-5 py-8 sm:py-10">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="ui mb-4 text-sm text-mute">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> › </span>
      <span>Methodology</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Methodology
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-body">
        Fail closed: if a figure is not in our fact file, it does not appear in
        generated prose.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-6 flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-4 text-body">
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold text-ink">Fact layers (GCU)</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-mute">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">College Scorecard</strong> (IPEDS unitid
          104717): enrollment, admission rate, SAT average, tuition, net-price
          inputs, completion, retention, median earnings, demographics, CIP
          program shares. Each value is stored with a source and as-of date.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Wikidata / Commons</strong>: founding year,
          coordinates, official site, campus photo and seal (CC or public domain
          only).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">HLC / DAPIP</strong>: institutional
          accreditation status and since-year. Programmatic accreditations only
          when we have a URL.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Editorial file</strong> (
          <code>official/gcu.json</code>): CTA URLs, Common App / ED flags,
          college list, degree levels, climate one-liner. Missing field → that
          heading is omitted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Map / climate / safety</strong>: OpenStreetMap
          static map; cited Phoenix climate; link to GCU’s annual security
          report (the PDF is not scraped).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Reddit</strong>: OpenAI web search restricted
          to reddit.com, then a live permalink check. Threads are labeled
          “Sourced from Reddit.” If search or the check fails, Reviews is
          omitted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Rankings</strong>: outbound profile links
          only. We do not republish U.S. News, Forbes, Niche, or Princeton
          Review integers or grades.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-bold text-ink">Generate / validate</h2>
      <p>
        Each prose heading is one model call, then a separate validation call,
        for at least three rounds. Any number that is not already in the fact
        JSON fails validation. The last passing draft is kept. Three failures
        omit the heading. Infobox numbers, logos, CTA hrefs, OSM, and comparison
        tables never go through the model.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-bold text-ink">Honest gaps</h2>
      <p>
        We do not invent an employment rate, live net-price calculator math,
        club or Greek lists, meal-plan menus, or a campus “political climate.”
        GCU’s IRS tax-exempt status, Education Department Title IV
        classification, and College Scorecard ownership code are different
        determinations; we do not collapse them into one label. Christian
        identity can differ between campus and online students.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-bold text-ink">What we skip</h2>
      <p>
        Portal, login, Halo, library, jobs, and logo-download pages belong on
        gcu.edu. We do not scrape gcu.edu, U.S. News, Forbes, Niche, or
        Princeton Review at grow time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
